  "body": "## What happens\n\nIn a 2D Offset with \"Pass starts at\" Outside, the ramp is made only when the \"Arc turn corners\" option is ON. With the option OFF, the ramp is not made.\n\nThe maintainer saw this in outside offset milling.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe entry and the ramp are a safety and a surface item. The choice of a corner option must not decide whether the operation ramps. With the option off, the pass starts without its ramp, so the entry becomes another move at the wall.\n\nIf that move is a plunge into uncut stock, this issue is `P1`. Confirm the first move on a fixture.\n\n## What to check\n\n- Does the corner rounding change the side plan, the ring count or the ring geometry in a way that removes the ramp?\n- The entry law of #3746 and #3748, and the create path of #3863, all read the start side. Show which of them reads the corner option, if any.\n- The pins of `pass_start_engagement` and `offset_pass_start` may not cover the pair (Outside, Arc turn corners off).\n\n## Missing at filing\n\n- The sketch, the tool and the exact first moves. Add them as a comment when the case is reproduced, then this issue can pin it.\n\nFound by the maintainer while testing outside offset milling. File with the readings when known.\n",
